{"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"module","title":"SnowplowEncoding","modules":[{"name":"SnowplowEncoding"}],"externalID":"SnowplowEncoding","roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Sending to Snowplow","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowSetupError"],"anchor":"Sending-to-Snowplow"},{"title":"Encoding batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder"],"anchor":"Encoding-batches"},{"title":"Records left out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowEncodingError"],"anchor":"Records-left-out"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:backoff:clock:)","isActive":true},{"text":" makes an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","isActive":true},{"text":") for a Snowplow pipeline in one call. It checks the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"collector’s URL, the Iglu vendor and the app ID, and posts to the collector’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/com.snowplowanalytics.snowplow\/tp2"},{"text":" endpoint with a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder","isActive":true},{"text":". It splits each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"batch to the limits of Snowplow’s own mobile trackers (","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","isActive":true},{"text":"): 25","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events and 40,000 bytes a request, with a larger event, of up to 150,000 bytes, in a request of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its own. A batch with no record the encoder can write, an empty one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"included, makes no request. The destination retries no response, a 5xx, 408 and 429, and drops","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and reports any other status. No trace context is sent. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"text":" leaves this module out;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"import it on its own.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A collector takes events from anyone who can reach it, so there is no key or secret, and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination builds on every platform: an app sends to the collector directly."}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import HTTPDestinations","import SnowplowEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let snowplow = try HTTPDestination.snowplow(","    collector: collector,  \/\/ https:\/\/collector.example.com","    vendor: \"com.example\",  \/\/ the Iglu vendor the plan is exported under","    appID: \"shop-ios\",","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: snowplow)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The factory throws "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowSetupError"},{"type":"text","text":" for a collector URL that isn’t "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"https"},{"type":"text","text":", that has no host,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a user name, a query or a fragment, or that already ends in the endpoint; for a vendor Iglu"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"doesn’t take; and for an empty app ID or one longer than 255 UTF-16 code units."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Schemas from the tracking plan","anchor":"Schemas-from-the-tracking-plan"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each event is a self-describing event: its data comes with the Iglu URI of the schema it must"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"match, and Snowplow’s pipeline validates it against that schema before loading it. The URI is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"named after the event and its version, under the vendor the destination is given:"}]},{"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing","code":["iglu:<vendor>\/<name>\/jsonschema\/<version>-0-0"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Version N of an event is SchemaVer "},{"code":"N-0-0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and events always name it. Raising an event’s version"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is a breaking change, which is SchemaVer’s MODEL. The export compares each event with the newest"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"schema of its version the registry holds, by what the two mean rather than their bytes, as the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"plan’s own check does:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An event that hasn’t changed keeps its published file, and nothing is written.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A breaking change at the same version, such as a property made required, is refused: raise the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event’s version.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A compatible change, such as an optional property added, is an ADDITION. For Iglu Server the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"export writes it as "},{"code":"N-0-1","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", then "},{"code":"N-0-2","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", each listing the earlier ones in "},{"code":"$supersedes","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Snowplow validates events naming "},{"code":"N-0-0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" against the newest, so a release already in users’"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hands keeps validating. Superseding needs Iglu Server 0.11.0 or later and Enrich 3.8.0 or later."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A static repository doesn’t support it: it would validate those events against "},{"code":"N-0-0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" alone,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so for one the export refuses the change, and the event needs a new version."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Write the registry from the plan with ","type":"text"},{"code":"TrackingPlan.writeIgluRegistry(to:vendor:registry:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"iglu <vendor> server|static <registry-directory>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" command of the tracking plan’s executable, or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the ","type":"text"},{"code":"export-tracking-plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plugin’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"--iglu-vendor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"--iglu-registry","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Then publish it with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"igluctl","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" before the release that sends the events.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"An event name Iglu takes holds only ASCII letters, digits, ","type":"text"},{"code":"-","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"_","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and the version must be 1","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or more. The encoder skips every record of an event that breaks either rule, and logs a notice for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each such event of the plan when the destination is made. The export refuses such an event too.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"What Snowplow receives","anchor":"What-Snowplow-receives"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each request is a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"payload_data"},{"text":" 1-0-4 array of events, one per record. Every event has:","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"e"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ue"},{"text":": a self-describing event, with its data in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ue_pr"},{"text":" as JSON text;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"eid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the record’s identifier, which a redelivered record keeps;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dtm"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ttm"},{"type":"text","text":", the record’s timestamp in milliseconds, so Snowplow’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"derived_tstamp"},{"type":"text","text":" is when"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the event was tracked;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"aid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the app ID; ","type":"text"},{"code":"p","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the platform; ","type":"text"},{"code":"tv","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; and ","type":"text"},{"code":"ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"0.0.0.0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"No ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stm"},{"text":" is sent: a retried request sends the same body again, so a sent time would be the first","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attempt’s, and Snowplow would move the event later by however long the retries took.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The standard context, when the record has it, goes in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"co"},{"type":"text","text":" as Snowplow’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mobile_context"},{"type":"text","text":" 1-0-3"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(the operating system, Apple as the manufacturer, the device model, the network type and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"language) and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"application"},{"type":"text","text":" 1-0-0 (the app’s version and build). The platform is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mob"},{"type":"text","text":" for a phone,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pad, watch or Vision Pro, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tv"},{"type":"text","text":" for an Apple TV, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pc"},{"type":"text","text":" for a Mac and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"app"},{"type":"text","text":" for a record with no device."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"type":"text","text":" the encoder is made with. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Only the session identifies a record","anchor":"Only-the-session-identifies-a-record"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The record’s session, from the sessions enricher, is its ","type":"text"},{"code":"sid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", Snowplow’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"domain_sessionid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nothing else identifies it. No ","type":"text"},{"code":"duid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"uid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"nuid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"tnuid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is sent, no ","type":"text"},{"code":"client_session","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"entity (its ","type":"text"},{"code":"userId","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lasts across sessions), and no IDFV, IDFA or other device identifier. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record’s vendor identifier and trace context aren’t sent either. A record with no session, from a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tracker without the sessions enricher, is sent without a ","type":"text"},{"code":"sid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; a record a store recovered after a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"relaunch keeps its session and its ","type":"text"},{"code":"sid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Snowplow’s mobile data models","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"read a session from the ","type":"text"},{"code":"client_session","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" entity, so set the unified package’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"snowplow__session_identifiers","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to ","type":"text"},{"code":"[{\"schema\": \"atomic\", \"field\": \"domain_sessionid\"}]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for these","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The collector would give each device an identifier of its own: it sets an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sp"},{"type":"text","text":" cookie, which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps and sends back, and records the request’s IP address. Every request carries"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SP-Anonymous: *"},{"type":"text","text":", so the collector sets and reads no cookie, records "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"network_userid"},{"type":"text","text":" as all"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"zeros, and records no IP address or forwarding header fields."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Records left out","anchor":"Records-left-out"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out and the rest of the batch is sent:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"one the plan doesn’t describe, whose event isn’t ","type":"text"},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or that holds a value JSON can’t;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"one whose event name Iglu doesn’t take, or whose version is below 1;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose timestamp falls outside the years 0 to 9999, which Snowplow’s enrichment fails;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"one whose JSON is over 150,000 bytes, which the smallest of a pipeline’s streams, SQS’s 192 kB,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"might not take with the request around it.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The destination reports each as "},{"code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", a "},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" whose reason is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowEncodingError","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"What the collector doesn’t report","anchor":"What-the-collector-doesnt-report"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The collector answers 200 to every request it can read and validates nothing. Snowplow checks the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events later, in enrichment. An event whose data its schema rejects, whose schema the pipeline’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Iglu resolver can’t find, or that is larger than the pipeline’s stream takes, becomes a failed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event: it is kept apart and never reaches the warehouse, though the destination counted it as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivered. Publish each schema before the release that sends it, and watch the pipeline’s failed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events after a change to the plan. Snowplow’s resolver caches schemas, for 10 minutes by default,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so a schema published after the first event that names it can still be missed for that long."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Snowplow doesn’t remove duplicates as events arrive. A record is sent more than once when a request","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is retried after the collector stored it but the answer was lost, when a delivery sends a cancelled","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"batch again, and when a store redelivers records after a relaunch. Each copy keeps its ","type":"text"},{"code":"eid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Snowplow’s data models, which deduplicate on ","type":"text"},{"code":"event_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", count it once.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers what Snowplow receives, and why, in more detail.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Send records to a Snowplow collector as self-describing events, whose schemas come from the tracking plan.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/snowplowencoding"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://SnowplowEncoding/documentation/SnowplowEncoding":{"url":"\/documentation\/snowplowencoding","kind":"symbol","title":"SnowplowEncoding","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to a Snowplow collector as self-describing events, whose schemas come from the tracking plan."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding","role":"collection","type":"topic"},"doc://SnowplowEncoding/documentation/SnowplowEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A destination that sends batches to the Snowplow collector at ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"collector"},{"text":", as self-describing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events whose schemas are ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"text":"’s under ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vendor"},{"text":", from the app ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"appID"},{"text":", through ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transport"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"retrying a send that fails for now with the waits of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"backoff"},{"text":" on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clock"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transport"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPTransport"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encoding"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SnowplowBatchEncoder"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},"url":"\/documentation\/snowplowencoding\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appid:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","title":"snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"snowplow"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"collector"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"URL","preciseIdentifier":"s:20FoundationEssentials3URLV"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"vendor"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"appID"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"plan"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"TrackingPlan","preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A4PlanV"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"transport"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Transport"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"backoff"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ExponentialBackoff","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations18ExponentialBackoffV"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"clock"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Clock","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Duration","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV"},{"kind":"text","text":">) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SnowplowSetupError","preciseIdentifier":"s:16SnowplowEncoding0A10SetupErrorO"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"HTTPDestination","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations15HTTPDestinationV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Transport"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SnowplowBatchEncoder","preciseIdentifier":"s:16SnowplowEncoding0A12BatchEncoderV"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)"},"doc://SnowplowEncoding/documentation/SnowplowEncoding/SnowplowEncodingError":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SnowplowEncodingError","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","title":"SnowplowEncodingError","url":"\/documentation\/snowplowencoding\/snowplowencodingerror","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Why ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder","type":"reference"},{"text":" couldn’t send a record, which it leaves out of the batch’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"requests as a ","type":"text"},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reports as a drop. When it can encode no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record of a batch, it makes no request, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sends nothing for the batch.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowEncodingError","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SnowplowEncodingError","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/choosingdestinations":{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","type":"link","title":"Choosing Destinations","titleInlineContent":[{"text":"Choosing Destinations","type":"text"}],"url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations"},"doc://SnowplowEncoding/documentation/SnowplowEncoding/SnowplowBatchEncoder":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder","title":"SnowplowBatchEncoder","url":"\/documentation\/snowplowencoding\/snowplowbatchencoder","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" of Snowplow’s tracker protocol, so an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can send events to a Snowplow collector’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"POST \/com.snowplowanalytics.snowplow\/tp2"},{"type":"text","text":", as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"self-describing events w